WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080
Start on the left. Our Banking Client
has seventy-five offshore quality

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:08.080
assurance staff, including
forty-five manual and domain testers.

00:00:08.224 --> 00:00:10.760
They share a few test environments.

00:00:10.825 --> 00:00:15.600
Backend services are not virtualized,
and vendor test slots limit parallel runs.

00:00:15.737 --> 00:00:20.480
Manual execution, reruns and evidence
collection add coordination work.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:24.640
The proposed target is
on the right. Squads reuse

00:00:24.696 --> 00:00:28.480
supported quality engineering
services: controlled test data,

00:00:28.542 --> 00:00:32.480
isolated runs, virtualized
dependencies and retained evidence.

00:00:32.656 --> 00:00:37.280
This foundation lets teams repeat service
tests without waiting for every vendor

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:42.240
slot. AI adds assistance with test
preparation and interpretation.

00:00:42.309 --> 00:00:46.480
People still approve expected behavior,
review generated changes and make

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.507
release decisions. Real provider
checks remain necessary.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:53.680
The next slide shows how we
will judge this architecture

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:56.320
through quality outcomes,
alongside effort.
